    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im lookin at a 2022 f-150 that's slipping under load. scanned it and the pressure readings in the hydraulic circuit are all over the place, getting these irregular spikes during shifts. what are the most likely causes for these pressure fluctuations in the transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in a 2022 F-150 under load are most likely caused by a failing transmission valve body, worn torque converter clutch seals, or low transmission fluid level causing aeration. Since the vehicle is specific to the 2022 model year, these fluctuations are often symptoms of the automatic transmission system struggling to maintain line pressure, which can lead to slipping; check your transmission fluid dipstick carefully first, as dehydration is a frequent culprit. If fluid levels are normal, inspect the transmission electronic control module (TCM) for fault codes that may indicate a malfunctioning solenoid or sensor. Always have a technician diagnose this with a factory scanner, as self-diagnosis on recent vehicles can be unreliable.",
