      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can use your factory 151D or equivalent factory-level scanner to enter the Transmission Control Module (TCM) live data parameters to monitor solenoid activation voltages and pump pressures while the vehicle is held in gear under load. This will show if a specific pressure pulse spikes when a solenoid should be switching, confirming a stuck or shorted solenoid versus a blockage which might show erratic pulses without consistent activation. A physical blockage usually manifests as a complete loss of pressure during a shift rather than an isolated voltage spike, but only a specialized transmission technician can confirm this definitively without further invasive testing.",
