    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the scanner is showing the solenoid voltage is right where it should be, but the pressure is still spiking way too high and then dropping off. it's almost like something is intermittently interfering with the flow or the sensor is just getting crazy readings. i've ruled out the obvious mechanical stuff, so i'm wondering if there's some kind of weird electronic glitch or internal debris causing this. any ideas on why the pressure would be so erratic if the voltage is stable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
