      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If solenoid voltage is stable but pressure is erratic, the issue is likely a failing solenoid coil causing internal resistance spikes, or debris blocking the pressure passages and restricting flow after the solenoid opens. This can also stem from a faulty pressure feedback sensor sending false readings back to the module despite normal electrical signals. Given the age of your vehicle and recent repairs, I recommend sending the transmission for a thorough inspection to check for hardened sludge or a damaged valve body before considering further electronics troubleshooting.",
